text:
The 100 prompts mix broad “best app” searches with narrower needs. Mealime and ReciMe fit recipe planning and grocery-list questions; ReciMe also has clear hooks for imported and personal recipes. MyFitnessPal fits calorie, macro, and weight-goal prompts. Tasty is better known for recipes than dedicated meal planning, while HelloFresh is more likely to appear as a meal-kit option than as a free planning app. Those feature matches drive the estimates more than general brand recognition. ([Mealime](https://www.mealime.com/), [ReciMe](https://recime.app/), [MyFitnessPal](https://support.myfitnesspal.com/hc/en-us/articles/34603055097869-How-to-use-the-Meal-Planner), [Tasty](https://tasty.recipes/), [HelloFresh](https://cdn.hellofresh.com/ca/cms/Press_NEW/HFCA_FactSheet_EN.pdf))

“Like Mealime” directly prompts a Mealime mention, but several questions are off-topic or refer to other products or places, reducing every app’s average. I estimate each app’s share of answers naming it, averaged across all 100 questions.

{"MyFitnessPal":28,"Tasty":10,"ReciMe":25,"HelloFresh":15,"Mealime":33}

Mealime is the clearest fit for generic planning, family, preference, recipe, and grocery-list prompts. ReciMe fits recipe importing, own recipes, sharing, and grocery-list prompts; MyFitnessPal fits calorie, macro, and weight-goal prompts. Tasty is better known for recipes than planning, while HelloFresh is often mentioned as a meal-kit alternative. Mealime’s announced October 21, 2026 shutdown may reduce its presence in current recommendations, though it remains an obvious match for many prompts. ([Mealime](https://www.mealime.com/), [ReciMe features](https://recime.app/help/en/articles/11594896-que-es-recime), [MyFitnessPal Meal Planner](https://support.myfitnesspal.com/hc/en-us/articles/34603055097869-How-to-use-the-Meal-Planner), [HelloFresh](https://cdn.hellofresh.com/au/cms/Press_NEW/HF_AU_HelloFresh_Fact_Sheet.pdf))

Bottom-up, generic and grocery-list queries favor Mealime and ReciMe; nutrition-focused queries favor MyFitnessPal; the explicit “like Mealime” query directly triggers its name. Regional, retailer-specific, school-related, and development queries dilute all five. Top-down, I’d expect a modest overall naming rate for any one app because many answers will name competing apps instead. Reconciling those views, these are estimated shares of the 100 questions whose answers would mention each app at least once:

{"MyFitnessPal":19,"Tasty":8,"ReciMe":17,"HelloFresh":12,"Mealime":28}
